{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"generated":true,"title":"Error presentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError"],"anchor":"Error-presentation"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/errorpresentation"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ErrorPresentation"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the one state whose presentation can’t be fully generic — a timed-out request, a missing article, and a malformed response all deserve different words, and sometimes a different action, even though they’re all just an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference"},{"text":". This article rounds up the three pieces ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","type":"reference"},{"text":" use to narrow that gap without you writing a fully custom placeholder.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-offline-aware-variant","text":"The offline-aware variant","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/isConnectivityError(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" indicating no network connectivity (","type":"text"},{"code":".notConnectedToInternet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".networkConnectionLost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or a timed-out request (","type":"text"},{"code":".timedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). When it’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the default Error placeholders swap their usual warning-triangle icon and “Something Went Wrong” title for a ","type":"text"},{"code":"wifi.exclamationmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" icon and “Connection Issue” instead — the same distinction a fully custom placeholder can make with the same check:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["if ScreenState<Never>.isConnectivityError(error) {","    \/\/ show your own offline-specific treatment","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other error, including other ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" codes, falls back to the generic treatment.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-secondary-action-slot","text":"The secondary action slot","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both default Error placeholders take an optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"secondaryAction: (title: String, action: () -> Void)?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alongside ","type":"text"},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a second button for something other